\tag{fcap}
\tag{spin}
\tag{clifford}

\taxon{Remark}
\title{Horizons beyond the exterior model
\citet{Section 3.2.4, Theorem 3.3, pp. 59--60}{meinrenken2013clifford};
\citet{Section 2.4, Theorem 8, pp. 286--287}{kostant1997clifford};
\citet{I.2, pp. 13--19}{lawson2016spin}}

\p{The exterior action constructed above now reaches diagonal weight lines
and the even/odd half-spin carrier decomposition in \ref{fcap-0025}.
Irreducibility of either summand requires further arguments. The cited
Tau Ceti weight and parity declarations do not assert irreducibility or
highest weights.}

\p{The generic mathematics of differentiating a smooth Lie-group
homomorphism is developed in \ref{fcap-001Q}. What remains missing for the
Spin cover is more specific: compatible Lie-group structures on TauCeti's
abstract #{\Spin(V)} and #{SO(V)}, followed by the identification of their
specialized differential with the algebraic quadratic action above. The open
TauCeti PR linked in \ref{fcap-001W} proposes only the generic Lie functor.}

\p{Highest weights and triality still belong to later layers. The abstract
Bott-periodic real algebra table is now recorded in \ref{fcap-0016};
\ref{fcap-0026} gives its signature-#{(1,3)} instance. Kostant supplies
the differential in the classical complex setting, and Lawson--Michelsohn
treat the real Pin and Spin groups. The remaining horizons do not follow
merely from the algebraic restrictions
#{\operatorname{spinRep}} and #{\operatorname{pinRep}}.}
